{
  "$comment": "The answer to docs/PLAN.md §13, and the bytes it was read off. The candidate word-geometry corpus does not say which KFGQPC print it paginates, and V1/1405H and V2/1421H disagree on 36 pages — so adopting the wrong one would invalidate ayah-pages.json, every edge's dPage and every share link, silently. `probe-ligature-print.mjs` compares its per-word data-surah/data-aya tags against ours, page by page, and this file records the verdict plus a SHA-256 per page fetched, so a rerun against the same pin either reproduces or says loudly that upstream moved. Not a pin in quran-svg.pin.json's sense: nothing here is vendored, because nothing here is adopted. Regenerate with `pnpm probe:ligature-print --write`.",
  "candidate": {
    "repo": "mushafdatabase/MushafDatabase-Ligature-Based-SVG",
    "url": "https://github.com/mushafdatabase/MushafDatabase-Ligature-Based-SVG",
    "commit": "ae5786ab08597f8123575dec4e774f1eca195e0f",
    "commitDate": "2026-06-13",
    "path": "SVG V1.01",
    "datasetVersion": "SVG V1.01 (data-md-version=\"1.01\"); the repo also carries SVG V1.0",
    "license": "Sadaqa-e-Jaria grant in the repo's LICENSE: use, copy, modify, publish, distribute and derive, for any lawful purpose including commercial, without prior written approval; must not alter the Quranic content in a way that misrepresents it; as-is, no warranty.",
    "sourceStatedInReadme": "KFGQPC Madinah Mushaf, Hafs 'an Asim, from the printing-use collection at https://dm.qurancomplex.gov.sa/ — the complex and the narration, but never the print revision, which is what this probe had to establish.",
    "wordGeometry": "Per-word <g id=\"md-word-NNN\"> carrying data-surah, data-aya, data-word-index-in-ayah, data-hafs, data-imlaey, data-line-number, wrapping per-ligature groups of <path data-text>. Paths, not rects: a word's box has to be measured or precomputed, not read off an attribute.",
    "size": "595 KB raw / 114 KB gz per page, measured over the 56 fetched. Projected over 604: 351 MB raw, 67 MB gz — 2.6x the shipped page corpus (26.2 MB gz), against a gate:assets pages ceiling of 32 MB."
  },
  "ranOn": "2026-08-04",
  "verdict": "same-print",
  "$verdict": "Every page checked carries exactly the ayahs our table puts on it, including all four bands where V1 and V2 are known to diverge. The candidate paginates KFGQPC QCF V2 / 1421H, the same print as quran-svg — so its page numbers are our page numbers, and word geometry is not blocked on the print question. What it is blocked on is coordinates: our page 120 is viewBox 0 0 345 550 under a flipping matrix, theirs is 0 0 382.68 547.09, so word boxes do not transfer without a per-page registration against the text block (theirs states one as data-rect on #md-page-inner).",
